**Summary:**
Authors propose novel algorithm for reinforcement learning with randomized exploration. Algorithm achieves minimax optimal regret bound up to poly-logarithmic factors, and it is the first such result for RL algorithms based not on the principle of Optimism in the face of Uncertainty. The most crucial algorithmic features that allow authors to achieve their result are
1) use a single Gaussian noise up to scaling for all transitions;
2) specific Bernstein-shaped magnitude of noise;
3) novel clipping procedure that was used at the first time for algorithms with randomized exploration.
